│      FRESHMAN = 1                                                  │
│      SOPHOMORE = 2                                                 │
│      JUNIOR = 3                                                    │
│      SENIOR = 4                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│      do_not_call_in_templates = True                               │
│                                                                    │
│      def __call__(self):                                           │
│          return self[/patched]                                     │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Explanation:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ I’ve added do_not_call_in_templates = True to the YearInSchool     │
│ class definition. This will instruct Django to prevent the         │
│ enumeration type from being called in templates, resolving the     │
│ issue described in the original problem. I've assumed models.py is │
│ the file containing the YearInSchool definition.                   │
